<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Tubman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1895">1895</a>–<a href="/years/1971">1971</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as William V. S. Tubman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Tubman was President of Liberia from 1944 until his death in 1971, the longest-serving president in its history. His open-door policy brought foreign investment in iron ore and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a>, and his unification policy extended rights to the indigenous majority, though power stayed with the Americo-Liberian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/true-whig-party">True Whig Party</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-tubman.jpg" alt="William Tubman" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anefo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Afdrukken_ANEFO_Rousel,_fotonummer_157-1166_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
